Workaround dev-libs/elfutils (libelf) bug 34468 by using the mmap ELF writer.

libelf's non-mmap elf_update() writer (ELF_C_RDWR) can overwrite a
section-header table that lives in a gap between section data, without
writing the (unchanged, non-dirty) section headers back. This corrupts
the ELF: the section-header string table entry gets zeroed and later file
offsets drift out of sync with their virtual addresses, so ldconfig reports
the library as "truncated".

It is triggered when patchelf places the section-header table in such a gap
(e.g. media-libs/opencv setting a long DT_SONAME like
libopencv_videoio_gstreamer.412.amd64.so) and portage's estrip then runs
debugedit -i to (re)compute the build-id, calling elf_update().

The ELF_C_RDWR_MMAP writer handles this layout correctly by skipping the gap.

Gentoo bug: https://bugs.gentoo.org/980264
elfutils bug: https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=34468

--- a/tools/debugedit.c
+++ b/tools/debugedit.c
@@ -3580,7 +3580,7 @@
   if (dest_dir == NULL && (!do_build_id || no_recompute_build_id))
     elf = elf_begin (fd, ELF_C_READ, NULL);
   else
-    elf = elf_begin (fd, ELF_C_RDWR, NULL);
+    elf = elf_begin (fd, ELF_C_RDWR_MMAP, NULL);
   if (elf == NULL)
     {
       error (0, 0, "cannot open ELF file: %s", elf_errmsg (-1));
